  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Navigation: route over the pole</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.7 (c) / Essential 2.3 (d): Compare the distance along a parallel with the great-circle route over a pole for two places on opposite meridians, and judge a claim about the shortest route.</p><p id="edition">Core and Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 3 (The sphere), Exercise E, question 3 of School Mathematics Project, SMP Book 5 (Metric), ed. P. G. Bowie, Cambridge University Press, 1969: parallel route against the route over the pole; a claim to criticise, new numbers.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core and Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
